  {
    "episode_id": 72696,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72696.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 13,
    "turn_text": "I support the move. Let me ask you this, Jeff. If you were making $1,300 a head, Would you be saying we want anybody watching over us? No, you'd say, man, this is a pretty good deal. Actually, you wouldn't be doing the right thing. What the president is trying to do here is make sure that there's competition in the marketplace. That's what he's trying to do. He knows that if we have strong ag markets, then we have a vibrant economy in rural America. And right now, we don't have strong ag markets because they're consolidated. And we can Pilgrim's Pride, prime example. I mean, they came in, they fixed prices, and they did get fined for it, but in the end, you know, when they're making $400 million bucks, $100 million fine, ain't much. And that's what they made off of that little scenario that they set up. So getting back to the president's order, I think the president is pitching in on this. I appreciate it. And now we need to get the special investigator passed. If we do that, there's some oversight on these big guys. And here's another thing I didn't bring up to you, Jeff, is that take a look at what happened to JBS here about a month or a month and a half ago, where we had some bad guys in Russia that came in and did a cyber attack on them. You know, they're one of the big four. They control 80% of the food. If you apply that back, 20% of our food is put at risk because of that. This is more than even more than just competition in the marketplace. It's also about national security because if people don't have food, you're in upheaval. So I appreciate what the president's done. I don't think it's enough. I think we need to get a couple bills that the grassland and I have passed. If we're able to do that, Then I think we're well on the way to making sure the markets will be more fair and we have competition.",
