  {
    "episode_id": 72696,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72696.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 17,
    "turn_text": "I'll be honest with you, I wish everything was able to be fattened on grass and not in the country, but we don't have the landmass for that. And so, you know, I'm also one of those guys that likes a good barley fat and beef. You throw that steak on the plate and it's pretty tough to beat. It's marbled up a little bit. And you get those from some of those animal feeding operations. But once again, you don't want them destroying your water. Water's critically important. You don't want them destroying anything. You want them to be good operators. And so I don't know that you can throw them all in the same in the same pot.",
